      "issue": "An expired row is borrowed under records lock, then admitted only after releasing that lock. Another owner may prune the row between lookup and admission. The borrowed row can start a fresh detached window while a later request for the same owner creates a second fresh window in the map.",
      "concreteInterleaving": [
        "A borrows ownerX expired row and pauses before synchronized(fetchRecord).",
        "B creates another owner, observes X expired and removes X during prune.",
        "A resets the detached X row and admits request1.",
        "C for ownerX creates a new in-map row and admits request2 within that same window."
      ],
      "impact": "For accessLimit1, two admissions can occur in one new interval; the original non-pruning map does not have this deletion race.",
      "minimalFix": "Serialize lookup/prune/window check and update under the same registry lock, or hold a real pin through admission. Keep actual Host scope/deadline checks outside registry critical work.",
